Nyckelharpa, Rhodes electric piano, upright or felt piano, bass trombone, muted trumpet, minimal-techno drum machine, mono sub synthesizer, rim percussion, restrained hi-hat, tape echo, short plate reverb, contact microphones, sympathetic-string pickups, relay samples, cabinet-roll recordings, paper movement, footsteps, and low room-tone capture.

For Fans Of: Mulatu Astatke’s modal economy, minimal techno in the Basic Channel lineage, contemporary Nordic bowed-string experimentation, The Necks’ patient repetition, and chamber-jazz ensembles that use acoustic resonance as structure rather than decoration.

